KNOWNBUG
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ class hidden by parameter: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [basic.lookup.qual.general]/1: lookup of N in N::b considers only
namespaces, types and templates whose specializations are types, so it
finds struct N although the parameter N hides it.  The front end finds the
parameter and leaves f's body incomplete ("could not fully type-check").  A
hidden namespace works.  test_enumeration.desc covers a scoped enumeration;
libc++'s __format_spec::__validate_*(__flags __flags) use `__flags::__second'
etc., so their bodies are dropped (__chrono/parser_std_format_spec.h:73-133
for <chrono>).  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program (-std=c++98), and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
